BT 1 0 0 1 38 588 Tm (Let Z=\(log X\)^\(1/4\) and Q_Z be the product of primes 67<=p<=Z. Define) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 579 Tm  T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 570 Tm (  B_Z\(X\) = SUM_\(d|Q_Z\) mu\(d\) b\(X/d\)/sqrt\(d\),) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 561 Tm (  U_Z\(X\) = B_Z\(X\)/sqrt\(X\).) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 552 Tm  T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 543 Tm (Using b\(Y\)=a_* sqrt\(Y\)+c_*+O\(Y^\(-3/2\)\) uniformly over d|Q_Z gives) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 534 Tm  T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 525 Tm (  B_Z\(X\) = a_* sqrt\(X\) PROD_\(67<=p<=Z\)\(1-1/p\)) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 516 Tm (           + c_* PROD_\(67<=p<=Z\)\(1-1/sqrt\(p\)\) + o\(1\),) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 507 Tm  T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 498 Tm (so B_Z\(X\)>0 for all sufficiently large X and U_Z\(X\) is comparable to 1/log Z.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 489 Tm  T* ET
